	affiliations = {Symbiosis Institute of Digital and Telecom Management, Pune, India},
	abstract = {Digital payment services employ secure electronic transactions to enable smooth monetary exchanges among individuals, corporations, and institutions. By utilizing encryption and authentication mechanisms, these services guarantee the preservation of data accuracy and privacy during the whole transaction process. Digital payment systems combine NFC, QR codes, and mobile apps to streamline transactions. Users may effortlessly transact on smartphones, tablets, and PCs. These services accept credit/debit cards, mobile wallets, and peer-to-peer transfers. This promotes financial inclusivity and improves the effectiveness of monetary transactions in the modern digital economy. Digital payments and mobile governance in India have greatly improved financial inclusion, government efficiency, and public involvement. India is moving toward a cashless economy and expanding access to public services through innovations such as UPI and smartphone applications, which are also promoting socio-economic growth and digital empowerment. This research articles covers the domains of Digital Payment Services and Governance that is made simplified by the advancement in telecom technologies. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
