	affiliations = {Banque du Canada, Currency Department, Ottawa, Canada},
	abstract = {In recent years, the rise in digital payments has spurred discussion about the future of cash at the point of sale. The COVID-19 pandemic has also contributed to this discussion. To better under¬stand cash acceptance and the impact of payment innovations such as mobile payments in Canada, the Bank of Canada conducted the 2021–22 Merchant Acceptance Survey Pilot Study — a survey of around 500 small and medium-sized businesses. We find that 97 per cent of small and medium-sized businesses in Canada accepted cash in 2021–22 and only 3 per cent have plans to stop accepting cash. For cards and digital pay¬ments, merchant acceptance has increased over the last few years. Therefore, cash and digital pay¬ments continue to co-exist at the point of sale, and Canada is far from being a cashless society. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
